Reason:
The bug occurs because if `io->bio` is NULL when the function checks if the `fio` is at the end of a zone, it leads to a NULL pointer dereference when attempting to call `bio_get(io->bio)`. This situation can happen if multiple threads have already submitted the `io->bio` before the function checks the zone end condition.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (f2fs_sb_has_blkzoned(sbi) && btype < META && is_end_zone_blkaddr(sbi, fio->new_blkaddr)) {
    bio_get(io->bio);
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves moving the zone end condition check before the `skip:` label, ensuring that the check for whether `fio` is at the end of a zone is performed for each `fio` before proceeding. This prevents the function from dereferencing a NULL pointer by ensuring that `bio_get(io->bio)` is only called when `io->bio` is guaranteed to be non-NULL.

